PR #503 Review (feat: migrate end-loop signal from marker file to session state)

Findings

1. MUST-FIX — "'`ralph` can mark unrecoverable-error exits as `completed`
- File: `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts:1802`
- Final session status is computed only from `consecutiveFailures >= maxFailures`.
- Unrecoverable exceptions outside the max-failures path still reach the `finally` block, and this code can close the session as `completed`, which conflicts with `@session-end-loop-signal ac-session-close-error` ("max failures or unrecoverable error" => abandoned with error reason).
- Recommended fix: set an explicit error `exitReason` / error flag for unrecoverable exits and compute close status from `exitReason`, not just the failure counter.

2. SHOULD-FIX — `task start` can be blocked by stale/completed sessions
- File: `src/cli/commands/task.ts:1117`
- The new end-loop guard checks only `end_requested` and ignores session status.
- Since `closeSession()` preserves `end_requested`, a stale `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` pointing to a completed/abandoned session can still block `kspec task start` even when no loop is actively ending.
- Recommended fix: interpret end-loop as blocking only for active sessions, or clear `end_requested` when closing the session.

3. SHOULD-FIX — AC coverage for unrecoverable-error close path is missing
- File: `tests/ralph/end-loop.test.ts:304`
- `ac-session-close-error` in the spec explicitly includes both max-failures and unrecoverable-error exits.
- The current tests only assert the `max_failures` branch and mostly via static source-string checks.
- Recommended fix: add a behavioral test covering an unrecoverable-error exit path and asserting session metadata closes as `abandoned` with a reason.

Checks run

- `gh pr diff 503`
- `gh pr view 503 --json title,body,files`
- `kspec task get @migrate-end-loop-to-session-state`
- `kspec item get @session-end-loop-signal`
- `kspec validate` (fails with unrelated repo-wide reference/alignment/completeness issues; filtered output did not show a PR-specific trait-AC coverage warning for this spec)

Notes

- The branch checked out locally is `feat/migrate-end-loop-to-session`.
- I did not run any long-running `kspec` processes (per ralph-loop safety constraints).
