  "body": "Found 3 issues in this PR.\n\n1. MUST-FIX: `ralph` can close a session as `completed` on unrecoverable error paths because final status is derived only from `consecutiveFailures >= maxFailures`. This misses the `ac-session-close-error` \"unrecoverable error\" case.\n2. SHOULD-FIX: `task start` blocks on any `end_requested=true` session, including already-closed sessions, so a stale `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` can incorrectly prevent task starts.\n3. SHOULD-FIX: test coverage for `ac-session-close-error` only checks the `max_failures` branch via static string assertions and does not cover the unrecoverable-error path called out by the spec.\n\nNotes:\n- `kspec validate` currently fails on many unrelated repo-wide reference/alignment/completeness issues (e.g. duplicate `@observations`), so I filtered the output and did not see a PR-specific trait-AC coverage warning for `@session-end-loop-signal`.\n- Branch checked: `feat/migrate-end-loop-to-session`.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/cli/commands/ralph.ts",
      "line": 1802,
      "body": "MUST-FIX: this status calculation only treats `max_failures` as an error (`consecutiveFailures >= maxFailures`). If the loop exits via any other unrecoverable exception before hitting that threshold (for example during iteration setup/teardown), `finally` still runs and closes the session as `completed`. That violates `ac-session-close-error` for the unrecoverable-error case. Please derive `abandoned` vs `completed` from an explicit error `exitReason` (or set an error flag) instead of only the failure counter."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/cli/commands/task.ts",
      "line": 1117,
      "body": "SHOULD-FIX: this blocks on `end_requested` without checking whether the session is still active. `closeSession()` preserves `end_requested`, so a stale `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` pointing at a completed/abandoned session will still block `task start` even though no loop is ending. Consider requiring `session.status === \"active\"` when interpreting the end-loop signal (or clearing the flag on close)."
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/ralph/end-loop.test.ts",
      "line": 304,
      "body": "SHOULD-FIX: `ac-session-close-error` covers \"max failures or unrecoverable error\", but this test only checks the `max_failures` branch with static string assertions. Please add a behavioral test (or at least a more direct integration-style test) for an unrecoverable-error exit path so the AC is actually covered."
    }
  ]
